WEBVTT

00:00:01.340 --> 00:00:08.430
As we cast our eyes above to the boundless sky, we know

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:16.480
Whatever tomorrow brings, the sun will always shine

00:00:17.230 --> 00:00:20.570
So won't you come with me?

00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:37.630
It's almost time for the school bell to ring

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:39.840
And every moment by moment

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:42.260
I feel more and more like I could fly

00:00:42.590 --> 00:00:45.720
This feeling fills my thoughts and sets my heart alight

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:49.180
It's this moment I love most of all

00:00:49.850 --> 00:00:53.850
In my bag I hold all the things I've overcome

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:57.610
And on their wings, I'll fly into the future

00:00:57.610 --> 00:01:02.110
We can do anything, at any time and any place

00:01:02.110 --> 00:01:05.610
And no one can stop us even if they try

00:01:05.780 --> 00:01:10.240
From ING and that alone can we proceed

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:14.160
Carrying all our feelings as we go

00:01:14.330 --> 00:01:18.170
Flying with our dreams for all to see

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:24.630
Let's close today's chapter, and start a new page!

00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:12.720
Sixteen-chan sure spends a lot of time taking care of her skin.

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:16.100
Well, she has her magazine work too,

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:19.350
but she gets little metal balls stuck in her pretty easily.

00:02:21.820 --> 00:02:23.400
What's wrong?

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:26.820
You should have said bullet fragments instead, or something.

00:02:26.820 --> 00:02:27.740
Huh?

00:02:27.740 --> 00:02:29.110
Why?

00:02:29.110 --> 00:02:30.820
Did I say something weird?

00:02:31.070 --> 00:02:33.330
Never mind. It's fine.

00:02:55.720 --> 00:02:59.900
I stayed in the bath too long while admiring Sixteen-chan taking care of her skin.

00:03:03.770 --> 00:03:07.360
You guys should make sure you take care of yourselves too.

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:09.860
I'll help you out.

00:03:29.680 --> 00:03:31.590
W-Wait, Sixteen-chan!

00:03:31.590 --> 00:03:32.510
Hold on!

00:03:35.510 --> 00:03:37.770
You can't do that to Funko-chan!

00:03:37.770 --> 00:03:40.730
Why?! I'm good with my hands!

00:03:40.940 --> 00:03:42.150
You just can't.

00:03:46.020 --> 00:03:47.440
Fine...

00:03:47.610 --> 00:03:49.240
Eighteen!

00:04:17.220 --> 00:04:20.680
We should probably think about cleaning up.

00:04:20.680 --> 00:04:22.440
Yeah.

00:04:23.980 --> 00:04:27.150
Eighteen-chan, your pants are always pretty loose.

00:04:27.150 --> 00:04:29.070
That's just how it is with me.

00:04:29.070 --> 00:04:31.740
My stock's loose, so...

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:34.110
Do you have any problems with it at school?

00:04:34.110 --> 00:04:36.160
Well, I get by.

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:38.450
I have some problems in the winter, though.

00:04:40.330 --> 00:04:41.370
<i>Does she...</i>

00:04:41.790 --> 00:04:43.170
<i>not wear anything underneath?</i>

00:04:43.420 --> 00:04:44.120
Huh?

00:04:49.670 --> 00:04:51.300
Sensei, good morning!

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:52.340
Hi.

00:04:52.340 --> 00:04:54.050
Good morning.

00:04:54.050 --> 00:04:55.300
Morning.

00:04:56.430 --> 00:04:59.140
This is our homeroom teacher.

00:05:05.150 --> 00:05:07.480
He's been at our school for a while now,

00:05:07.480 --> 00:05:09.400
but it doesn't look like he's gotten used to it yet.

00:05:15.950 --> 00:05:17.820
Sorry, Sensei. My bad.

00:05:17.820 --> 00:05:19.530
Don't leave your bullets in the hallway like they're balls or something!

00:05:19.530 --> 00:05:20.830
Someone could get hurt!

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:23.830
He just said "balls"!

00:05:24.290 --> 00:05:25.500
Sensei's a pervert!

00:05:25.500 --> 00:05:26.580
That's sexual harassment!

00:05:26.580 --> 00:05:27.960
Now, look here...

00:05:29.460 --> 00:05:32.670
Hey! These are empty shells!

00:05:33.340 --> 00:05:35.840
How many times do I have to tell you not to fire in the classroom?!

00:05:35.840 --> 00:05:36.840
Ouch!
How many times do I have to tell you not to fire in the classroom?!

00:05:36.840 --> 00:05:39.350
I wasn't firing in the classroom! Honest!

00:05:39.350 --> 00:05:40.140
You telling the truth?

00:05:40.850 --> 00:05:42.220
Just in the hallway...

00:05:42.390 --> 00:05:43.680
Ow!

00:05:45.190 --> 00:05:47.520
Don't hit us! You're gonna leave a dent!

00:05:50.570 --> 00:05:51.780
Seriously...

00:05:57.360 --> 00:05:59.910
Why are you hiding, FNC?

00:06:02.040 --> 00:06:02.870
Well...

00:06:03.580 --> 00:06:06.080
You look like you're in a bad mood.

00:06:07.250 --> 00:06:08.580
I'm fine.

00:06:10.710 --> 00:06:12.590
<i>He got me again...</i>

00:06:12.590 --> 00:06:17.550
Oh yeah, I need to head over to the high school for a meeting about the seaside school.

00:06:17.550 --> 00:06:19.010
Wanna come along?

00:06:19.930 --> 00:06:21.050
Sure.

00:06:21.390 --> 00:06:25.600
There's still a lot I don't know about this school.

00:06:29.230 --> 00:06:30.440
So...

00:06:30.810 --> 00:06:32.570
you're an FNC, right?

00:06:33.440 --> 00:06:35.190
What are you talking about?

00:06:35.190 --> 00:06:39.160
Well, when I do roll call, you're listed as "Funko".

00:06:40.030 --> 00:06:42.080
Fal-neechan came up with that name out of the blue,

00:06:42.080 --> 00:06:44.330
and she's made everyone else use it.

00:06:44.330 --> 00:06:45.370
What a pain.

00:06:45.870 --> 00:06:48.080
You don't like your nickname?

00:06:48.080 --> 00:06:49.960
Of course not!

00:06:49.960 --> 00:06:50.880
I mean,

00:06:51.420 --> 00:06:52.670
it's weird, isn't it?

00:06:52.670 --> 00:06:53.500
"Funko".

00:06:53.670 --> 00:06:54.880
You think?

00:06:54.880 --> 00:06:56.800
I think it's cute.

00:06:57.510 --> 00:06:58.760
Makes you sound like a parrot.

00:06:59.590 --> 00:07:01.260
Cute?

00:07:01.260 --> 00:07:05.640
In that case, you're the only person who's allowed to call me Funko!

00:07:05.640 --> 00:07:08.600
Um, doesn't everyone already call you that, though?

00:07:12.400 --> 00:07:13.570
That reminds me...

00:07:13.570 --> 00:07:16.780
Doesn't M16 have a different nickname for you?

00:07:17.150 --> 00:07:18.280
"Fukko" or something.

00:07:18.780 --> 00:07:20.950
Sixteen-chan's my best friend.

00:07:20.950 --> 00:07:22.620
She may not look it, but she's actually really nice.

00:07:22.620 --> 00:07:25.660
She gave me a new name to replace the name I didn't like!

00:07:25.660 --> 00:07:28.000
I didn't expect that.

00:07:28.790 --> 00:07:29.960
Oh yeah,

00:07:30.580 --> 00:07:32.960
I was really surprised when I found this.

00:07:34.790 --> 00:07:38.090
I wrote "Funko", but I made a mistake,

00:07:38.090 --> 00:07:40.760
and when I read it back, I remembered it differently.

00:07:48.180 --> 00:07:49.640
I can't tell her that now.

00:07:49.640 --> 00:07:50.770
Yeah. Yeah.

00:07:58.940 --> 00:08:02.570
The high school has a completely different feel to it.

00:08:02.570 --> 00:08:04.700
It looks rather dignified.

00:08:11.620 --> 00:08:12.750
Fal-neechan!

00:08:15.670 --> 00:08:17.210
What is it, Funko?

00:08:17.210 --> 00:08:19.710
Oh, Sensei's here too.

00:08:19.710 --> 00:08:20.920
I'm helping him find his way.

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:22.510
Hi there.

00:08:22.510 --> 00:08:25.010
Is my sister giving you any trouble?

00:08:25.010 --> 00:08:26.760
Oh, you're...

00:08:27.180 --> 00:08:29.390
Sixteen's older sister, Fourteen.

00:08:29.390 --> 00:08:32.190
Despite my little sister’s looks, I’m pretty cute.

00:08:32.190 --> 00:08:33.480
Just kidding.

00:08:37.610 --> 00:08:39.980
I wonder if someone's talking about me.

00:08:39.980 --> 00:08:42.070
Here you go, G Cutie.

00:08:42.070 --> 00:08:43.280
For your nose.

00:08:47.740 --> 00:08:49.870
What's with the "G Cutie"?

00:08:49.870 --> 00:08:51.160
Beats me...

00:08:51.160 --> 00:08:54.580
That's what all the underclassmen call you.

00:08:55.040 --> 00:08:57.420
They're not talking about G3?

00:08:57.420 --> 00:08:59.090
I wonder why.

00:08:59.090 --> 00:09:00.550
Funko-chan, do you know?

00:09:00.550 --> 00:09:03.260
N-No, not really...

00:09:03.260 --> 00:09:06.340
Well, it doesn't sound that bad.

00:09:06.340 --> 00:09:07.720
I am pretty cute, after all.

00:09:07.720 --> 00:09:09.470
Maybe the G stands for "Great". For "Great Cutie".

00:09:09.470 --> 00:09:10.720
Who knows...

00:09:10.720 --> 00:09:13.270
Or maybe it's for "Gorgeous".

00:09:13.270 --> 00:09:16.350
So gorgeous you want to <i>gorge</i> yourself on the sight of me.

00:09:18.940 --> 00:09:20.530
<i>It stands for "God, not again."</i>

00:09:20.530 --> 00:09:21.820
<i>"God, not again."</i>

00:09:21.820 --> 00:09:23.190
<i>The "God, not again" Cutie.</i>

00:09:23.820 --> 00:09:25.110
<i>I can't tell her that.</i>

00:09:26.360 --> 00:09:28.910
So what does the G in G3 stand for?

00:09:29.240 --> 00:09:31.120
Well, it can't stand for "Great".

00:09:31.120 --> 00:09:32.950
You're the last person I want to hear that from.

00:09:33.330 --> 00:09:35.210
Maybe it stands for "Grade"?

00:09:35.210 --> 00:09:37.960
No, it's from the German word: <i>Gewehr</i>.

00:09:37.960 --> 00:09:39.540
It translates as "rifle".

00:09:40.670 --> 00:09:41.710
I see.

00:09:41.710 --> 00:09:42.760
What about you, Fal?

00:09:43.970 --> 00:09:46.760
It's French for <i>Fusil Automatique Léger</i>.

00:09:47.010 --> 00:09:49.180
Basically an acronym for "Light Automatic Rifle".

00:09:49.180 --> 00:09:54.640
And since it means "Light Automatic Rifle", people in English-speaking countries gave it the acronym "LAR".

00:09:54.890 --> 00:09:57.350
What about the L in L1A1?

00:09:58.020 --> 00:09:59.770
I see the letter A around a lot,

00:09:59.770 --> 00:10:01.610
but L is pretty rare.

00:10:01.860 --> 00:10:02.980
I don't know.

00:10:02.980 --> 00:10:05.150
There are lots of theories, but no one knows for sure.

00:10:05.150 --> 00:10:08.660
I was born in Belgium, but actually used in England,

00:10:08.660 --> 00:10:10.830
so it might stand for "land", as in "land forces".

00:10:11.700 --> 00:10:13.330
That's pretty complicated.

00:10:17.290 --> 00:10:20.710
We got in trouble when the Japanese teacher found the shells I left behind.

00:10:22.090 --> 00:10:24.130
And you weren’t shooting, so you did nothing wrong.

00:10:25.800 --> 00:10:28.970
A-Anyway, I'm going to find him.

00:11:23.020 --> 00:11:26.650
Once again, I have shot a worthless object.

00:11:30.030 --> 00:11:31.570
What's going on?

00:11:31.570 --> 00:11:32.990
She's using her gun like a samurai sword.

00:11:33.320 --> 00:11:35.950
Normally she'd only be able to pick off single targets,

00:11:35.950 --> 00:11:39.080
but by using her gun as a sword, she can shoot in a line.

00:11:39.500 --> 00:11:42.250
Just like a sword, she can use the speed and centrifugal force of the swing

00:11:42.250 --> 00:11:44.790
to nullify recoil from her full auto mode.

00:11:44.790 --> 00:11:47.550
It's a high-level submachine gun technique.

00:11:51.260 --> 00:11:55.350
I guess Sig-chan's the only one who an score a head shot

00:11:55.350 --> 00:11:57.140
from 50 meters out, though.

00:11:57.970 --> 00:12:01.270
The greater the centrifugal force, the lower the recoil.

00:12:01.270 --> 00:12:03.310
But as a result, your accuracy goes down,

00:12:03.310 --> 00:12:05.020
so you have to have the knack for it.

00:12:05.860 --> 00:12:06.520
So.

00:12:07.030 --> 00:12:09.030
Why is that useful?

00:12:09.740 --> 00:12:11.780
You can draw things a long way away.

00:12:11.780 --> 00:12:13.160
Like on the enemy camp.

00:12:15.950 --> 00:12:17.660
It's nice and peaceful here, isn't it?

00:12:44.600 --> 00:12:46.690
Guess I'll sit in the sun for a while.

00:12:47.320 --> 00:12:49.730
The sun is my friend.

00:12:52.200 --> 00:12:53.570
The sun...

00:12:56.780 --> 00:13:01.620
Did you know that ultraviolet light degrades plastic parts?

00:13:01.620 --> 00:13:04.120
The sun's an enemy of your skin, huh?

00:13:06.830 --> 00:13:08.840
Hey, Elle!

00:13:11.460 --> 00:13:13.010
I cleared you of all suspicion!

00:13:13.680 --> 00:13:15.840
Sorry about that, L85.

00:13:15.840 --> 00:13:18.050
I ended up hitting you too...

00:13:34.900 --> 00:13:39.030
I think she's <i>thinking</i> a lot of angry thoughts about you.

00:13:39.370 --> 00:13:40.450
She is?

00:13:40.450 --> 00:13:42.120
I'm really sorry.

00:13:42.120 --> 00:13:43.960
I'll buy you a drink as an apology.

00:13:45.040 --> 00:13:45.960
I love you.

00:13:46.580 --> 00:13:48.040
I'll take a cola!

00:13:48.040 --> 00:13:49.170
You get nothing!

00:13:56.130 --> 00:13:57.680
Come on!

00:14:01.220 --> 00:14:02.520
Sorry!

00:14:11.770 --> 00:14:16.740
Today the middle school is leading a volunteer trash pickup with the elementary school.

00:14:20.950 --> 00:14:22.830
Thompson-sensei!

00:14:23.290 --> 00:14:25.040
Good morning!

00:14:25.500 --> 00:14:27.210
Good morning.

00:14:27.210 --> 00:14:30.290
Thanks for your help today, everyone.

00:14:30.750 --> 00:14:31.460
You're welcome!

00:14:32.210 --> 00:14:33.920
Elementary students,

00:14:33.920 --> 00:14:38.260
make sure you listen to what your middle-school big sisters tell you, okay?

00:14:38.260 --> 00:14:41.430
Okay, Thompson-sensei!

00:14:42.430 --> 00:14:45.220
Let's have fun today, everyone!

00:14:45.220 --> 00:14:49.060
Now let's go pick up some trash!

00:14:49.060 --> 00:14:50.230
Yay!

00:14:50.520 --> 00:14:55.190
Row, row, row your boat.

00:14:55.190 --> 00:14:57.650
La, la, la, la, gently down the stream.

00:14:57.650 --> 00:14:59.820
<i>All the submachine guns go to elementary school.
La, la, la, la, gently down the stream.</i>

00:14:59.820 --> 00:15:01.280
<i>All the submachine guns go to elementary school.</i>

00:15:02.660 --> 00:15:05.620
The submachine gun is a category of firearm

00:15:05.620 --> 00:15:07.660
based on the <i>Maschinenpistole</i> utilized

00:15:07.660 --> 00:15:11.670
by the Germans at the end of World War I.

00:15:11.670 --> 00:15:14.420
They're capable of firing many bullets consecutively like an assault rifle,

00:15:14.420 --> 00:15:16.380
but they use pistol rounds instead.

00:15:16.380 --> 00:15:19.090
While their range and power specs are limited,

00:15:19.090 --> 00:15:24.060
they're rather portable, and provide good suppression fire in enclosed areas.

00:15:30.310 --> 00:15:32.360
She's a middle schooler, isn't she?

00:15:32.690 --> 00:15:33.610
Yeah...

00:15:34.440 --> 00:15:35.940
Wait up!

00:15:35.940 --> 00:15:38.150
Gossan uses different bullets from us!

00:15:38.360 --> 00:15:40.740
But then Gossan's dad told her that she had to go to grade school

00:15:40.740 --> 00:15:42.570
because she's got a small body, even though she's fully automatic.

00:15:42.570 --> 00:15:44.160
That's why she's in our class.

00:15:44.160 --> 00:15:47.080
But she uses the same rifle bullets you do.

00:15:47.080 --> 00:15:48.200
You got all that?!

00:15:53.750 --> 00:15:55.250
What happened?

00:15:55.250 --> 00:15:57.710
Don't sweat it.

00:15:57.710 --> 00:16:00.380
Emten-chan just ran out of bullets.

00:16:00.380 --> 00:16:04.100
She can fire 1,090 rounds a minute, you see.

00:16:05.140 --> 00:16:06.640
I see...

00:16:06.640 --> 00:16:07.060
Wait!

00:16:07.600 --> 00:16:10.350
You look exactly like G3-senpai!

00:16:11.310 --> 00:16:13.270
She's pretty short, though.

00:16:13.650 --> 00:16:15.360
G3's my sister.

00:16:15.360 --> 00:16:18.780
I'm MP5A2, attending elementary here.

00:16:18.780 --> 00:16:20.150
Please call me Empi.

00:16:20.610 --> 00:16:22.150
A little G3.

00:16:22.150 --> 00:16:23.910
She's a smaller version of G3.

00:16:23.910 --> 00:16:25.200
How cute.

00:16:25.200 --> 00:16:26.450
A <i>Wee</i>-3.

00:16:27.200 --> 00:16:30.540
Please try to remember my name, at least.

00:16:35.500 --> 00:16:36.460
Okay!

00:16:36.460 --> 00:16:38.050
Everyone listen up!

00:16:38.050 --> 00:16:40.720
We're going to start cleaning the river.

00:16:41.050 --> 00:16:44.930
Break up into your designated groups and listen to your leader!

00:16:45.260 --> 00:16:47.140
Are there any questions?

00:16:47.140 --> 00:16:47.930
Over here.

00:16:48.430 --> 00:16:51.140
Is Sixteen-senpai not coming?

00:16:56.690 --> 00:16:59.360
<i>Sixteen-chan, let's go do the volunteer trash pickup.</i>

00:16:59.360 --> 00:17:00.480
<i>Huh?</i>

00:17:00.480 --> 00:17:02.360
<i>Volunteer trash pickup?</i>

00:17:02.360 --> 00:17:03.400
<i>I can't make it.</i>

00:17:04.740 --> 00:17:08.530
<i>But you're really popular with the little kids, Sixteen-chan.</i>

00:17:08.740 --> 00:17:11.910
<i>I can't stand looking after kids.</i>

00:17:11.910 --> 00:17:14.500
<i>Tell the sensei I said hello.</i>

00:17:14.790 --> 00:17:16.540
Settle down!

00:17:18.090 --> 00:17:18.880
Um...

00:17:19.800 --> 00:17:21.710
Sixteen-chan is skipping this activity!

00:17:23.550 --> 00:17:25.300
<i>I made things worse.</i>

00:17:27.090 --> 00:17:31.560
Well, instead of Sixteen-chan, we have Elle-chan here to lead us.

00:17:34.770 --> 00:17:36.020
Question!

00:17:36.020 --> 00:17:37.730
Yes, what is it?

00:17:37.730 --> 00:17:42.490
Why is Elle-senpai still being used by the British army?

00:17:43.030 --> 00:17:46.160
You break after being fired a hundred times, right?

00:17:46.160 --> 00:17:47.320
No, you're wrong.

00:17:47.320 --> 00:17:50.240
They just throw the gun away after they've fired it a hundred times.

00:17:50.240 --> 00:17:52.120
I... Um...

00:17:52.120 --> 00:17:56.290
Or maybe they just retreat after firing a hundred shots...

00:17:57.210 --> 00:18:00.840
It's not nice to make things up, kids.

00:18:03.210 --> 00:18:05.380
Wh-What? It's all true?

00:18:06.880 --> 00:18:10.180
In the 1940s, the English were the first country

00:18:10.180 --> 00:18:13.270
to realize that shorter bullets coupled with lower caliber rifles

00:18:13.270 --> 00:18:14.730
would become the weapon of choice.

00:18:15.480 --> 00:18:19.690
With help from defecting Belgian and Czechoslovakian scientists,

00:18:19.690 --> 00:18:24.570
they started researching low caliber and bullpup rifles.

00:18:24.900 --> 00:18:28.160
Bullpup rifles differ from standard rifles

00:18:28.160 --> 00:18:30.870
by having their mechanics built into their stock,

00:18:30.870 --> 00:18:33.540
basically resulting in a more compact version of the weapon.

00:18:33.910 --> 00:18:35.750
The greatest advantage of this type of gun

00:18:35.750 --> 00:18:38.830
is that the length of the barrel is contained within the casing.

00:18:38.830 --> 00:18:43.550
In other words, the gun's size is reduced without sacrificing range.

00:18:44.090 --> 00:18:45.380
For guns that use the same bullets,

00:18:45.380 --> 00:18:48.220
the gun with the longest barrel can shoot farthest.

00:18:49.930 --> 00:18:52.680
But due to the lack of resources after World War II,

00:18:52.680 --> 00:18:55.560
new rifles couldn't be developed to replace older models.

00:18:55.560 --> 00:19:00.310
During that time, the Soviet Union manufactured shorter bullets for their SKS rifles.

00:19:01.150 --> 00:19:02.770
